# Inlang regenerates this directory on every paraglide compile, and ignores all of
# it but settings.json through a project.inlang/.gitignore of its own — which
# prettier never reads, because --ignore-path only covers the ROOT .gitignore. So
# a fresh checkout fails `prettier --check .` on .meta.json and README.md, while a
# local tree passes: an earlier `--write` reformatted them in place, and being
# git-ignored the change never showed up. Mirrors inlang's own rule.
project.inlang/*
!project.inlang/settings.json
